# Add project specific R8 rules here.
# AGP will combine all keep rule files in src/main/keepRules to pass to R8
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# Shrink and optimise, but keep names. Obfuscation buys nothing for an open-source app, and
# it costs three things here: stack traces in logcat stop being readable, the navigation
# back stack is saved by serialised class name (a rename between two builds would fail to
# restore it), and JNA below finds everything by name.
-dontobfuscate

# JNA. Its native dispatch library calls back into these classes by name over JNI, and reads
# Structure fields and Callback methods reflectively, so R8 can see none of the uses.
-keep class com.sun.jna.** { *; }
-keep class * implements com.sun.jna.** { *; }
# JNA's desktop-only AWT helpers, which Android does not have.
-dontwarn java.awt.**

# The generated UniFFI bindings to liboura_core.so. JNA binds the `UniffiLib` interface to
# the library's symbols by method name, and lays out `RustBuffer` and the other Structures
# from their fields, so the whole package is reached reflectively.
-keep class uniffi.** { *; }

# Room creates a database by reflection: Class.forName("<Database>_Impl").newInstance().
# Room 2.5.0, which WorkManager 2.9.1 brings in, keeps those classes but not their
# constructors, and R8 strips a constructor nothing calls directly. The first release build
# crashed at startup on 2026-11-15 creating WorkManager's own WorkDatabase.
-keep class * extends androidx.room.RoomDatabase { <init>(); }

# The same gap in WorkManager 2.9.1's own rules: an InputMerger is created by class name
# with its no-argument constructor before every job. With it stripped, each job fails with
# "Could not create Input Merger" — no crash, but no background sync and no widget refresh.
-keep class * extends androidx.work.InputMerger { <init>(); }
